Each file keeps the copyright notice it was published with.

RFC 1459 (May 1993)
-------------------

RFC 1459 predates the Internet Society copyright statement used in later
RFCs. Its status section says:

    Distribution of this memo is unlimited.

The document does not include a separate copyright statement.


RFC 2810, RFC 2811, RFC 2812, and RFC 2813 (April 2000)
-------------------------------------------------------

These four documents carry the Internet Society full copyright statement
reproduced below. The same text is included at the end of each file.

    Copyright (C) The Internet Society (2000).  All Rights Reserved.

    This document and translations of it may be copied and furnished to
    others, and derivative works that comment on or otherwise explain it
    or assist in its implementation may be prepared, copied, published
    and distributed, in whole or in part, without restriction of any
    kind, provided that the above copyright notice and this paragraph are
    included on all such copies and derivative works.  However, this
    document itself may not be modified in any way, such as by removing
    the copyright notice or references to the Internet Society or other
    Internet organizations, except as needed for the purpose of
    developing Internet standards in which case the procedures for
    copyrights defined in the Internet Standards process must be
    followed, or as required to translate it into languages other than
    English.

    The limited permissions granted above are perpetual and will not be
    revoked by the Internet Society or its successors or assigns.

    This document and the information contained herein is provided on an
    "AS IS" basis and THE INTERNET SOCIETY AND THE INTERNET ENGINEERING
    TASK FORCE DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
    BUT NOT LIMITED TO ANY WARRANTY THAT THE USE OF THE INFORMATION
    HEREIN WILL NOT INFRINGE ANY RIGHTS OR ANY IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF
    MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.


RFC 7194 (August 2014)
----------------------

RFC 7194 was published under BCP 78 and the IETF Trust Legal Provisions
in effect on its publication date. That was Trust Legal Provisions 4.0
(effective 28 December 2009, obsoleted 25 March 2015). The text is in
IETF-TLP-4.0.pdf in this directory.

    https://trustee.ietf.org/license-info
    https://trustee.ietf.org/wp-content/uploads/IETF-TLP-4.pdf

The copyright notice in the document is:

    Copyright (c) 2014 IETF Trust and the persons identified as the
    document authors.  All rights reserved.

    This document is subject to BCP 78 and the IETF Trust's Legal
    Provisions Relating to IETF Documents
    (http://trustee.ietf.org/license-info) in effect on the date of
    publication of this document.  Please review these documents
    carefully, as they describe your rights and restrictions with respect
    to this document.
